    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Kaiware</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> (a Japanese term for \"open shell\") refers to Daikon radish sprouts, often cultivated as microgreens. </span><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Purple Kaiware</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> (or Purple Radish microgreens) featurestriking magenta-to-purple stems and deep purple leaves. They deliver a highly concentrated, bold, and peppery radish flavor. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Grown by:Gorge Greens in Washington</span></p>",
